<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Package xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
    Companion manifest for manifest/portfolio-deal-b5/destructiveChangesPost.xml.

    STATUS: PREPARED, NOT AUTHORISED. Do not deploy without the user's explicit
    go-ahead. Nothing in Phase B5 has been deployed to any org.

    Phase B5 (FINAL) of the "Property Package -> Portfolio Deal" rename program
    retires the legacy Property_Package__c object. This half carries everything
    that must STOP REFERENCING the old object, plus the new object's own UI
    surface. It lands FIRST; the destructive half runs POST. See that file for
    the deletion list, the sweep evidence and the ordering rationale.

    CustomApplication (1): Acquisition
      Its `View` actionOverride is REPOINTED, not supplemented:
        was  Property_Package_Record_Page / pageOrSobjectType Property_Package__c
        now  Portfolio_Deal_Record_Page   / pageOrSobjectType Portfolio_Deal__c
      Both halves of that swap are one file edit and cannot be split across two
      waves: an actionOverride naming a FlexiPage or object that the destructive
      half deletes would fail the whole CustomApplication deploy. There is no
      CustomTab for either object (verified against the repo's tabs/ directory
      and the org), so this override is the ONLY route to a Portfolio_Deal__c
      record page, and removing the old one is what actually makes the old page
      unreachable.

    Flexipage (1): Portfolio_Deal_Record_Page
      NEW. A FlexiPage's <sobjectType> is not editable in place, so retiring the
      object forces a new page rather than a repoint. Structural clone of
      Property_Package_Record_Page, which the destructive half deletes.

    Layout (1): Portfolio_Deal__c-Portfolio Deal Layout
      This is an UPDATE, not a create. Salesforce auto-created a stock layout
      named exactly "Portfolio Deal Layout" when Portfolio_Deal__c was deployed
      in Phase B1 -- re-confirmed for B5 by a live Tooling query on 2026-08-18,
      which returned exactly one Layout per object ("Portfolio Deal Layout" on
      Portfolio_Deal__c, "Property Package Layout" on Property_Package__c).
      Matching that name is what makes this file update the stock layout instead
      of leaving the object with two layouts. The old layout is NOT in the
      destructive file; it cascades with its object.

    PermissionSet (4): every set that still named Property_Package__c
      Each drops its Property_Package__c grants in this wave. The org would drop
      those entries by itself when the object is deleted, but these FILES would
      not, and a permission set whose XML names a field or object that no longer
      exists fails the deploy of the whole set the next time anyone touches it.
      Scope is unchanged by the rename -- one grant for one grant on all four:
        - DPEG_Acquisition_Edit      6 fields + 3 lookups + objectPermissions, all editable
        - DPEG_Acquisition_View      6 fields + 3 lookups + objectPermissions, read-only
        - Broker_Protection_Access   6 fields + 1 Lead lookup + objectPermissions, editable
        - DPEG_Admin_Access          4 fields + 1 Lead lookup, NO objectPermissions
      DPEG_Admin_Access is deliberately the narrowest of the four and must stay
      that way: its scope was set by a 2026-08-17 code review against a MEASURED
      admin visibility gap on the Lead Funnel homepage, and it carries no
      objectPermissions because `Modify All Data` on the System Administrator
      profile already confers object level access. Do not "harmonise" it with the
      other three; that would overturn a documented decision under cover of a
      rename.

    NOT INCLUDED, deliberately:
      - DPEG_Apex_Access: its only Portfolio Deal change (classAccesses repointed
        to PortfolioDealController) belongs to Phase B4 and is already live in
        usman-dpeg. It names neither the old object nor the old fields, so B5
        does not touch it and does not need to redeploy it.
      - Portfolio_Deal__c (the object) and its 6 fields: created and deployed in
        Phases B1/B2, confirmed present in usman-dpeg by an EntityDefinition
        query on 2026-08-18. Unchanged by B5.
      - Apex and LWC: renamed and deployed in Phase B4 (DeployRequest
        0Afiw000000LpYzCAK). Re-verified clean of live Property_Package__c
        references for B5; the only remaining mentions are comments and one
        cosmetic test method name.

    A PERMISSION SET DEPLOY REPLACES ITS ENTIRE fieldPermissions SET rather than
    merging into it. That is exactly the behaviour this wave wants (it is how the
    old grants get removed), but it also means these 4 files must be the complete
    intended state for their objects at deploy time, not a delta. Retrieve and
    diff them against the org before the real deploy if any time has passed.

    Deploy (only once authorised by the user; devops runs a validation-only
    dry-run first per standing project practice):
      sf project deploy start \
        --manifest manifest/portfolio-deal-b5/package.xml \
        --post-destructive-changes manifest/portfolio-deal-b5/destructiveChangesPost.xml \
        --target-org usman-dpeg \
        --test-level RunLocalTests --wait 30

    Do NOT pass --purge-on-delete -- documented as non-functional on production
    orgs and fails silently rather than erroring (see manifest/portfolio-deal-a3).

    FOLLOW-UP THIS MANIFEST DOES NOT DO: the legacy source files still exist on
    disk (objects/Property_Package__c/**, the 3 lookup .field-meta.xml files under
    Lead / Opportunity / Property__c, flexipages/Property_Package_Record_Page,
    layouts/Property_Package__c-Property Package Layout). A --manifest deploy
    ignores them, so they cannot break THIS wave -- but any later
    `--source-dir force-app` deploy would recreate the object this wave deletes.
    They must be removed from the repo in the same commit that lands B5.
    -->
    <types>
        <members>Acquisition</members>
        <name>CustomApplication</name>
    </types>
    <types>
        <members>Portfolio_Deal_Record_Page</members>
        <name>Flexipage</name>
    </types>
    <types>
        <members>Portfolio_Deal__c-Portfolio Deal Layout</members>
        <name>Layout</name>
    </types>
    <types>
        <members>DPEG_Acquisition_Edit</members>
        <members>DPEG_Acquisition_View</members>
        <members>Broker_Protection_Access</members>
        <members>DPEG_Admin_Access</members>
        <name>PermissionSet</name>
    </types>
    <version>67.0</version>
</Package>
